	<description>&lt;b&gt;The magnificent second novel from the legendary author of &lt;i&gt;One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest...&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; Following the astonishing success of his first novel, &lt;i&gt;One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest&lt;/i&gt;, Ken Kesey wrote what Charles Bowden calls "one of the few essential books written by an American in the last half century." This wild-spirited tale tells of a bitter strike that rages through a small lumber town along the Oregon coast. Bucking that strike out of sheer cussedness are the Stampers. Out of the Stamper family's rivalries and betrayals Ken Kesey has crafted a novel with the mythic impact of Greek tragedy.</description>
